<title>JAPAN: Zedillo asks Japan for $1 bln loan for oil project.</title>
<headline>Zedillo asks Japan for $1 bln loan for oil project.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican President Ernesto Zedillo has asked Japan to extend loans for the development of offshore oil fields in the Gulf of Mexico, a Foreign Ministry official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>During talks with Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto, Zedillo requested a loan of about $1 billion from the Export-Import Bank of Japan for development of the Cantarell oil fields, the official said.</p>
<p>The Foreign Ministry official quoted Hashimoto as saying the bank was looking into the economic and technical aspects of the project and had not yet reached a decision.</p>
<p>Cantarell is Mexico's most lucrative crude source and is being developed by state oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (PEMEX).</p>
<p>Earlier this month, PEMEX announced plans to invest $5 billion and drill 164 new wells in the Cantarell oil fields by 2000. Zedillo's official visit to Japan ends on Friday.</p>
</text>
